"""apple-podcast-transcript — Apple Podcasts TTML extractor package source.

Reviewed extractor package source (protocol revision 3). Serves ONE request:
a revision-3 `ExtractorProtocolRequest` JSON object on stdin and JSON Lines
frames on stdout. The request carries a validated Apple Podcasts episode URL
(inputTransport "remote-url") — no input bytes exist.

Workflow:
  - With staged host support (the signed `podcast-token-helper`, staged by
    the host into the private operation root for this exact reviewed
    revision): acquire a bearer token (via the staged helper, cached in the
    host-owned revision-scoped token cache), call the Apple AMP transcripts
    endpoint, retry ONCE with a forced token refresh on Apple error 40012,
    download the access-keyed TTML, and convert it to Markdown with the same
    semantics as the former Swift parser.
  - Without staged host support: run the RSS transcript algorithm (iTunes
    lookup → feed → <podcast:transcript> attachment; VTT/SRT/HTML/plain).

The RSS path runs ONLY when no helper was staged. A failure after the helper
was staged never falls back to RSS — the failure frame is the report.

Failure messages are bounded and never contain the source URL, the helper
path, the bearer token, or any transcript/feed bytes.
"""

